Chapter: GazeSpec
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Geom
  cites Safari chapter Pose
  cites Safari chapter Pigs
  cites Safari chapter World
  cites Safari chapter Gaze
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 Gaze: whether the rider is looking at the pigs, where his head is turning, and
 how narrow the lens has gone because of it.

 FOUR SEPARATE REASONS NOT TO LOOK, and they are graded one at a time because
 each is a different refusal reaching the same answer. The leg has no distraction
 herd; his eyes are already off the road into a corner; the pig is further than
 he looks; or it is so close beside him that the bearing has swung past the
 release angle. A chapter collapsing any two of them would still show a rider
 who mostly looks at the right moments.

 THE LAST ONE IS THE INTERESTING ONE. He releases the pig not by distance but by
 ANGLE -- once it is more than thirty-five degrees off his heading he faces front
 again, which is what makes him turn back as he draws level rather than at some
 written-down range. On a four-hundred-metre leg the pig sits at 342 and twelve
 metres off the road, so at 200 he is looking and at 341 he is not, and nothing
 between those changed except the geometry.

 THE HEAD SWIVELS TOWARD AND DRIFTS BACK, at different rates and by different
 rules. Toward the pig is a fixed rate clamped both ways; back to the road is
 proportional, so it lingers and then decelerates, with the last sliver SNAPPED
 to zero rather than approached forever. All three behaviours are graded.

 THE FOCUS HOLDS ITS PEAK while the head is turned and eases only once he is
 straight, which is why it is a max against its own previous value rather than a
 function of the angle alone.

 We say:

Section: The Constants

  fixed-got : List Real
  fixed-got =
    [ gaze-look-dist, focus-decay, pig-gaze-speed, pig-gaze-settle-dist,
      gaze-release-angle / deg, gaze-swivel-rate / deg, gaze-return-rate / deg,
      gaze-return-snap / deg, eyes-on-road-yaw / deg, gaze-return-ease ]

  fixed-want : List Real
  fixed-want = [150.0, 0.0012, 0.2, 25.0, 35.0, 4.0, 0.2, 0.02, 6.0, 0.05]

  smooth-got : List Real
  smooth-got = [smoothstep 0.0, smoothstep 0.5, smoothstep 1.0, gaze-focus 0.5]

  smooth-want : List Real
  smooth-want = [0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 0.5]

Section: Looking Or Not

 Segment 2 is a distraction leg; segment 0 is not. The pig sits at 342 along and
 twelve metres off the road.

  plain : Segment
  plain = segment-at 0

  distracting : Segment
  distracting = segment-at 2

  rider : Real, Real -> RiderState
  rider (along) (yaw) =
    RiderState { segment = 2, along = along, across = 0.0, yaw = yaw, v = v-base,
                 tilt = 0.0, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0 }

  legs-got : List Boolean
  legs-got = [plain.pigs-distract, distracting.pigs-distract]

  legs-want : List Boolean
  legs-want = [False, True]

 The four refusals, then the case that looks.

  looking-got : List Boolean
  looking-got =
    [ (pig-ahead (rider 200.0 0.0) plain).looking,
      (pig-ahead (rider 200.0 (10.0 * deg)) distracting).looking,
      (pig-ahead (rider 100.0 0.0) distracting).looking,
      (pig-ahead (rider 341.0 0.0) distracting).looking,
      (pig-ahead (rider 200.0 0.0) distracting).looking,
      no-look.looking ]

  looking-want : List Boolean
  looking-want = [False, False, False, False, True, False]

 Looking carries the distance to the pig, and not looking carries a zero rather
 than a stale one.

  dist-got : List Real
  dist-got =
    [ (pig-ahead (rider 200.0 0.0) distracting).dist,
      (pig-ahead (rider 100.0 0.0) distracting).dist,
      no-look.dist ]

  dist-want : List Real
  dist-want = [142.0, 0.0, 0.0]

 THE WANT IS A BEARING AND NOT A FIXED ANGLE, so his gaze tracks the pig as he
 creeps past it -- and it is a LITERAL zero when he has no interest, which is
 what lets the swivel test it bitwise.

  want-got : List Boolean
  want-got =
    let far = desired-gaze (rider 200.0 0.0) distracting
    in let near = desired-gaze (rider 320.0 0.0) distracting
    in [far > 0.0, near > far, desired-gaze (rider 200.0 0.0) plain ~0 0.0]

  want-want : List Boolean
  want-want = [True, True, True]

Section: The Swivel

 Toward the pig at a fixed rate, clamped both ways, so a large want moves the
 head exactly one step.

  head : Real, Real -> RiderState
  head (gaze-yaw) (along) =
    RiderState { segment = 2, along = along, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, v = v-base,
                 tilt = 0.0, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = gaze-yaw, focus = 0.0 }

  swivel-got : List Real
  swivel-got =
    [ next-gaze-yaw (head 0.0 200.0) 1.0 - gaze-swivel-rate,
      next-gaze-yaw (head 0.0 200.0) (0.0 - 1.0) + gaze-swivel-rate,
      next-gaze-yaw (head 0.0 200.0) (gaze-swivel-rate / 2.0) - gaze-swivel-rate / 2.0 ]

  swivel-want : List Real
  swivel-want = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]

 Back to the road is PROPORTIONAL and capped, so it lingers at a large angle and
 decelerates as it straightens -- and the last sliver is snapped to zero rather
 than approached forever.

  return-got : List Boolean
  return-got =
    let big = next-gaze-yaw (head (30.0 * deg) 200.0) 0.0
    in let small = next-gaze-yaw (head (2.0 * deg) 200.0) 0.0
    in [ big < 30.0 * deg, big > 0.0, small < 2.0 * deg, small > 0.0,
         30.0 * deg - big > 2.0 * deg - small ]

  return-want : List Boolean
  return-want = [True, True, True, True, True]

  snap-got : List Real
  snap-got =
    [ next-gaze-yaw (head gaze-return-snap 200.0) 0.0,
      next-gaze-yaw (head (0.0 - gaze-return-snap) 200.0) 0.0,
      next-gaze-yaw (head 0.0 200.0) 0.0 ]

  snap-want : List Real
  snap-want = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]

Section: The Focus

 It rises with the turn and HOLDS its peak, so a head coming back does not take
 the lens with it; only a fully straight head lets it ease, and it never goes
 below zero.

  focused : Real, Real -> RiderState
  focused (focus) (gaze-yaw) =
    RiderState { segment = 2, along = 200.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, v = v-base,
                 tilt = 0.0, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = gaze-yaw, focus = focus }

  focus-got : List Boolean
  focus-got =
    let rising = next-focus (focused 0.0 (20.0 * deg)) (20.0 * deg)
    in let held = next-focus (focused 0.9 (1.0 * deg)) (1.0 * deg)
    in let easing = next-focus (focused 0.9 0.0) 0.0
    in [rising > 0.0, held >= 0.9, easing < 0.9, easing > 0.0]

  focus-want : List Boolean
  focus-want = [True, True, True, True]

 A straight head at zero focus stays at zero rather than going negative, and a
 head turned past the release angle saturates at one.

  focus-ends-got : List Real
  focus-ends-got =
    [ next-focus (focused 0.0 0.0) 0.0,
      next-focus (focused 0.0 (90.0 * deg)) (90.0 * deg) ]

  focus-ends-want : List Real
  focus-ends-want = [0.0, 1.0]

Section: The Gawk Gate

 He is not gawking until he has NOTICED the pigs, and from then on he is -- so
 the gate is a position and not the same test as looking.

  gawk-got : List Boolean
  gawk-got =
    [ gawk-engaged (rider 200.0 0.0) plain,
      gawk-engaged (rider 100.0 0.0) distracting,
      gawk-engaged (rider 200.0 0.0) distracting,
      gawk-engaged (rider 341.0 0.0) distracting ]

  gawk-want : List Boolean
  gawk-want = [False, False, True, True]

 THE GATE OUTLASTS THE LOOK, which is the pair worth having side by side: at 341
 he has long since faced front again and he is still gawking, because the brake
 holds him slow past the pig rather than releasing when his head does.

  outlast-got : List Boolean
  outlast-got =
    let looks = (pig-ahead (rider 341.0 0.0) distracting).looking
    in [looks == False, gawk-engaged (rider 341.0 0.0) distracting]

  outlast-want : List Boolean
  outlast-want = [True, True]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "gz-fixed " fixed-got fixed-want 0.000000000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "gz-smooth" smooth-got smooth-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "gz-legs  " legs-got legs-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "gz-look  " looking-got looking-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "gz-dist  " dist-got dist-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "gz-want  " want-got want-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "gz-swivel" swivel-got swivel-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "gz-return" return-got return-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "gz-snap  " snap-got snap-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "gz-focus " focus-got focus-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "gz-fends " focus-ends-got focus-ends-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "gz-gawk  " gawk-got gawk-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "gz-outlst" outlast-got outlast-want)
  end
